# Reference Shape v34

Unapproved shading concept generated with built-in image generation. User accepted v33 direction, rejected its invented repetitive shapes. This iteration reduces repeated small volumes and restores broader uneven crowns, long low banks and connected shadow planes. Approximation rather than exact traced reference. Not packed cloud/opacity data; no level replacement.

## Prompt

Create corrected grayscale polar UV cloud artwork. Image 1 is the ABSOLUTE SHAPE AND SHADOW REFERENCE. Image 2 conveys ONLY correct circumferential orientation; its cloud shape and repetitive bubbly texture were REJECTED. Do not reproduce image 2's evenly scalloped donut silhouette.
Faithfully study image 1: enormous quiet continuous cloud wall on right with asymmetrical broad irregular plateaus, short uneven humps on tops, deep broad saddle between tall towers, long nearly flat low stretches; not a string of round ball clouds. The rightmost cloud top is a sloping broad shoulder with small ragged lobes. Middle-right has a lower uneven mass then a broad taller flat-ish tower. Small left horizon clouds have very low long bases, few unequal small rises, long thin horizontal layers. Preserve those recognizable proportions, asymmetry and silhouette rhythms. Cloud bodies have huge almost unbroken gray/blue-gray shadow planes; sparse pale cream cap planes and just two or three irregular connected shadow boundaries. Remove 90 percent of image 2's little scalloped internal marks. Shadow shapes should match broad silhouettes in image 1, not concentric rings and not round cells.
Conceptually trace cloud shapes from image 1, erase text/house/terrain/characters, reconstruct only hidden small portions, then BEND THE WHOLE LONG HORIZONTAL CLOUD STRIP onto polar coordinates: original horizontal axis follows circumference, original upper direction points toward center, original underside points outward. DO NOT invent new tower patterns. Dominant tall banks on right perimeter; long low banks along left and lower perimeter, plenty of black center. At right all originally horizontal long shelves and shadow layers run VERTICALLY AND CURVE ALONG CIRCUMFERENCE. At bottom run horizontally, at left run vertically. NO screen-horizontal tongues pointing into central sky. Each whole silhouette/shadow rotates with its angular position. Keep approved direction of image 2 while replacing silhouette and painting with actual image1 shapes.
One square grayscale cloud shading concept, pure BLACK empty sky and margin. Flat restrained hand-painted animation sky clouds, almost solid broad tonal planes, subtle transitions only. No realistic cauliflower, repeated puff balls, brush stamps, white rim lines, decorative strokes, arrows, lettering, checkerboard or scene objects. Outer base gently softened but readable, irregular not perfect circular cut.
